3. NVMe VARIANT — boot-probe: PASS (acceptance gate 3)
================================================================================

Invocation:
  SPONGE_BOOT_NVME=1 make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-boot \
      KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc RUN_OPT="--include image/disk ..."

QEMU drive attach line (proves the NVMe device is a separate disk):
  qemu-system-x86_64 ... -device pcie-root-port,id=root_port1 \
      -drive id=disk0,file=bin/nvme_disk.img,format=raw,if=none \
      -device nvme,drive=disk0,serial=fnord,id=nvme0,bus=root_port1 \
      -drive format=raw,file=var/run/sponge-boot.img \
      -machine q35 ...

The boot .img auto-attaches to AHCI (boot media only); the NVMe disk
(bin/nvme_disk.img, a separate 32 MiB GPT disk with P3 GENODE ext2) is
the storage target.

