================================================================================
4. FAILURE PATH — bounded, stage-identified (acceptance gate 4)
================================================================================

Method: Built a normal .img, extracted P3, removed /system/marker.txt via
e2rm, wrote P3 back. Booted QEMU against the modified image with a 90s
timeout (no run_genode_until — manual QEMU invocation).

Result: The failure was IDENTIFIED at the "rom_fetch" stage and BOUNDED
(the probe stopped immediately — no silent hang):

  [init -> ahci]         #0: ATA                           ← driver OK
  [init -> part_block] GPT Partition 3: ... 'GENODE'        ← partition OK
  [init -> vfs] rump: /genode: file system not clean; please fsck(8)
                                                          ← mount WARNING (mounted anyway)
  [init -> cached_fs_rom] Error: /marker.txt not found     ← STAGE IDENTIFIED: rom_fetch
  [init -> boot_probe] Error: stop because parent denied ROM-session: \
      label="marker.txt", , ram_quota=6K, cap_quota=3      ← PROBE STOPPED (bounded)
  qemu-system-x86_64: terminating on signal 15 (timeout)   ← 90s hard bound

The probe did NOT hang — it received the ROM-session denial and exited.
Init kept running (other components alive); the 90s timeout killed QEMU.

================================================================================
5. VARIANT RECOMMENDATION (product-media primary)
================================================================================

RECOMMENDATION: AHCI as the product-media primary.

Rationale:

1. **Single-disk simplicity.** With AHCI, the boot media IS the storage
   target. image/disk's auto-attach (`-drive format=raw,file=X`) lands on
   the q35 AHCI controller; the ahci driver binds it; part_block reads P3
   from the same disk GRUB booted from. One disk, one controller, one
   Block session. The NVMe variant required a SEPARATE disk image
   (bin/nvme_disk.img) attached via -device nvme — the boot .img on AHCI
   is only the boot media, and its P3 goes unused. This complicates media
   creation (tool/dist must produce TWO disk images or a hybrid layout).

2. **Boot-from-storage.** Real USB media presents as AHCI/SATA to the
   firmware. SeaBIOS (the default q35 firmware) boots from AHCI but NOT
   from NVMe. An NVMe-primary product would require UEFI (OVMF) firmware,
   adding a host dependency and a different boot path. AHCI-primary keeps
   the BIOS + GRUB chain that the Alpha already uses.

3. **Both work on seL4.** docs/14 §11 risk 1 flagged ahci on base-sel4 as
   "analogy-proven, not demonstrated." P1 has now DEMONSTRATED it: two
   consecutive PASS runs with exact byte validation. The NVMe driver
   (already seL4-proven via nvme.run) also passes, confirming the docs/14
   §3 risk assessment.

4. **NVMe remains the escape hatch for real hardware.** On real PCs with
   NVMe-only storage (no AHCI/SATA ports), the NVMe variant is the path.
   The run script's `SPONGE_BOOT_NVME=1` switch documents this: the same
   scenario, the same chain, just a different Block driver and QEMU attach
   line. P2+ should verify the NVMe path on real hardware before locking
   it as the primary for a specific device target.

docs/14 §11 risk 1 mitigation status: CLOSED for AHCI (demonstrated on
seL4). NVMe also demonstrated (was already proven via nvme.run).

================================================================================
6. ADVERSARIAL CLASS ADDRESSES
================================================================================

misleading_success_output:
  - The run_genode_until regex matches BOTH "boot-probe: PASS" AND the
    marker string "sponge-boot-marker-v1". A bare exit 0 or a garbage
    PASS line does not match.
  - The probe prints the actual marker bytes in the PASS line: (22 bytes:
    "sponge-boot-marker-v1."). The QEMU drive attach lines are logged
    above (§2, §3).
  - The marker content is exact-compared (22 bytes, byte-identical to the
    string staged in the run dir). No trailing newline, no padding
    accepted as content.

hung_or_long_commands:
  - Every run_genode_until has a bounded timeout (120s for the success
    gate; the failure-path QEMU used a 90s `timeout` wrapper).
  - The probe calls env.parent().exit() on both PASS and FAIL — it never
    lingers after its check completes.
  - The failure path (§4) shows the probe stopped immediately on ROM
    denial — no silent hang.

stale_state:
  - var/run/sponge-boot was cleaned between every variant run (rm -rf
    var/run/sponge-boot*).
  - The test image is rebuilt fresh each run (image/disk creates a new
    .img from the current run dir contents).
  - bin/nvme_disk.img is created fresh for each NVMe run and cleaned up
    at the end (exec rm -f bin/nvme_disk.img).

